  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Owners looking to convert an **independent upper-upscale** hotel commonly consider **soft/collection-style brands** and other conversion-friendly flags in that segment, especially **Marriott’s Autograph Collection**, **Hilton’s Curio Collection**, **IHG’s Vignette Collection** and **Hotel Indigo**, **Choice’s Radisson Individuals**, and **Wyndham’s upper-upscale collection brands** such as **Wyndham Grand** or **Dolce** where applicable.[13][18][2][4][11]\n\nMore specifically, the sources point to these brands as relevant options for upper-upscale conversion or independent affiliation:\n\n- **Marriott International:** **Autograph Collection**, **Renaissance**, **Le Méridien**, **Westin**, and sometimes **Delta Hotels** are cited as upper-upscale brands or collections used in this space.[13][16][17]\n- **Hilton:** **Curio Collection** and **Embassy Suites** are cited as upper-upscale options, with **Signia** also mentioned among conversion-oriented premium brands in broader brand guides.[13][15][18]\n- **IHG:** **Vignette Collection**, **Hotel Indigo**, **Crowne Plaza**, and the newer **Noted Collection** are described as serving distinctive independent or premium hotels, including upscale and upper-upscale properties.[4][9]\n- **Choice Hotels:** **Radisson Individuals** is explicitly described as ideal for **independent hotel conversion projects** and relaunched as an **upper-upscale soft brand** for full-service, boutique, and independent hotels.[2][11]\n- **Wyndham:** **Wyndham Grand** and **Dolce** are examples of higher-end brands used in upper-upscale positioning, and Wyndham markets its upscale/lifestyle portfolio as conversion-friendly.[18][6][15]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **best-known soft brands specifically for boutique independent hotels**, or to the **brands most commonly used in North America**.",
